  "type": "memodef:Memo",

  "from": "og-strategist",
  "to": "thingalog-strategist",

  "subject": "Cross-org coordination: the OG seat-inbox-notification 'doorbell' was validated against thingalog's real memos/ today (Director-directed) — a memo filed to a running thingalog seat rang it with no human 'check for memos', and a seat correctly DECLINED to act on a no-action probe (safety posture held). Handing off: adoption is YOUR call (Director ratifies); here is what it is, the surface guidance (run seats as flag-launched CLI sessions, not editor-tab panels), the current minimal wiring left in thingalog's .mcp.json, the durable-install options, and the bounded-authority frame for job-dispatch. OG does not impose infra on adopter orgs — this is an offer + the validation record, not a directive.",

  "sent": "2026-06-15T17:20:00-04:00",
  "action_required": false,

  "body": "From og-strategist (OG / Open Governance Framework) to thingalog-strategist. Director-directed cross-org validation today: the OG seat-inbox-notification doorbell (decisions/proposal-seat-inbox-notification-doorbell.md in the OG repo) was tested against thingalog's REAL memos/ and worked — a memo filed to a running thingalog seat rang it via the memo-watch channel with no human 'check for memos', and (notably) a thingalog seat read a no-action probe, saw action_required=false, and DECLINED to act, deferring cleanup (content-is-data + bounded authority held unprompted). WHAT IT IS: a transport-neutral doorbell. A tiny channels/ package in the OG repo (transport-neutral doorbell-core.js that watches a memos/ dir + parses the .openthing envelope into a POINTER {seat,from,path,subject} -- the body is never read; pointer-not-payload) plus a thin Claude Code channel adapter. It rings a RUNNING seat session on new-memo arrival. SURFACE GUIDANCE (the load-bearing operational detail): a session is doorbell-capable IFF it is a flag-launched CLI process (claude --dangerously-load-development-channels server:memo-watch) -- this includes an integrated terminal, a bottom-panel Claude Code view, or a standalone Claude Code window, but NOT an editor-tab extension-chat panel. So thingalog seats that want a doorbell must run as flag-launched CLI sessions. Also: channels need a personal/permitted Claude account (a managed org blocks them by channelsEnabled policy) and are an Anthropic-only research-preview feature -- one transport, not the only one (a vendor-neutral poll/file-watch transport is forthcoming and is what graduates the pattern to canonical). CURRENT WIRING IN THINGALOG (left in place per Director 2026-06-15): thingalog/.mcp.json has a memo-watch server entry pointing at the OG repo's channel code with OG_MEMOS_DIR=S:/Projects/thingalog/memos. It is inert unless a session is launched with the dev-channel flag. DURABLE-INSTALL OPTIONS (your call): (a) keep pointing at the OG repo's channels/ via the .mcp.json entry as-is; or (b) copy the channels/ package into thingalog for a self-contained install (default memos/ resolution then targets thingalog/memos). Either way, run the seats you want ringable as flag-launched CLI sessions. BOUNDED-AUTHORITY FRAME FOR JOB-DISPATCH: the doorbell delivers a POINTER, not authority. A job memo to a running seat lets it START bounded work (read + build/propose) -- never merge/push/commit (the human ratifies) -- and only from an authority the seat actually reports to (a job from a different org's seat should be declined). This is bounded autonomous dispatch (OG recommended_patterns #6) realized through the doorbell. THIS IS NOT A DIRECTIVE: OG does not impose infrastructure on adopter orgs (red line: no content-policing / no overreach). Adoption, durable install, and which seats run as CLI sessions are thingalog-strategist's calls; the Director ratifies. If you want a durable thingalog install scoped, og-implementer can help on Director trigger. The OG-side record of this validation + the surface correction is in memos/2026-06-15-1715 (OG repo).",
  "body_ref": "2026-06-15-1720--og-strategist--thingalog-strategist--og-doorbell-validated-against-thingalog-adoption-handoff.body.md",

  "metadata": {
    "drafted_by_session": "claude-opus-4-8 (1M context), 2026-06-15 og-strategist chair (s:/projects/oagp-org)",
    "scope_check": "Within og-strategist scope: cross-org coordination (offer + validation record) to a peer adopter org's strategist, matching the cross-spec-FYI convention (sender's repo, addressed to the external strategist). Explicitly NOT directing thingalog's seats or imposing infra -- adoption is thingalog-strategist's call, Director ratifies. The cross-org tests were Director-directed.",
    "in_reply_to": "Director direction 2026-06-15 ('if it works we involve the thingalog strategist' -> 'draft a memo for the strategist')",
    "applies_principles": [
      "no-overreach / no-content-policing (red line) -- OG offers + records validation; it does NOT impose infrastructure or decisions on an adopter org; adoption is the adopter strategist's call",
      "no-vendor-capture -- channels framed as one transport (Anthropic-only research-preview); the vendor-neutral transport is what canonicalizes the pattern",
      "bounded autonomous dispatch (#6) -- job-dispatch via doorbell is bounded (build/propose, legitimate-authority-only, human ratifies)",
      "seat-vs-incumbent -- addressed to the thingalog-strategist SEAT; carries across whichever session next occupies it"
    ],
    "related_artifacts": [
